{% comment %}
  Rebrand person hero — the head of a teacher page and of an artist page.
  Same anatomy in both comps: the name in large IvyPresto on the left, a
  subtitle under it, a social row, and on the right a large artwork running
  off the right edge with a black-and-white portrait set into it.

  The two differ only in the subtitle and the palette:
    Teacher — coral name, a row of medium tags, an Instagram round icon and a
              "See Portfolio" pill.
    Artist  — moss name, a line of Cedarville script, Instagram only.

  On a collection template the name and artwork default to the collection, so
  an artist or teacher collection is correct as soon as it gets the template.

  The picture is the comp's artwork-plus-inset by default; "media_mode" can put
  the artist's photo there on its own instead, which is what the artist pages
  now do. See the comment above that setting.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'saf-rebrand.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign sid = section.id
  assign name = section.settings.name | default: collection.title

  comment
    The comp shows a row of mediums under a teacher's name. The catalogue
    already carries them as medium-* product tags, so an empty field reads
    them off the collection rather than leaving the row blank or, worse,
    repeating one person's mediums on everyone else's page.
  endcomment
  assign tag_source = section.settings.tags
  if tag_source == blank
    assign mediums = ''
    for t in collection.all_tags
      assign lower = t | downcase
      if lower contains 'medium-'
        assign label = lower | remove_first: 'medium-' | replace: '-', ' ' | capitalize
        unless mediums contains label
          assign mediums = mediums | append: ',' | append: label
        endunless
      endif
    endfor
    assign tag_source = mediums | remove_first: ','
  endif
  assign tags = tag_source | split: ','

  comment
    The two comps put different things under the name: the teacher gets this
    row of mediums, the artist gets a line of script. "auto" therefore shows
    the row only on a page that carries no script line.

    The teacher pages are set to "always": the client asked for the artist
    comp's script line on that side of the page as well, and the mediums are
    the one thing on a teacher's page that says what they actually make, so
    they carry both — script first, then the row, as the markup runs.

    Until 2026-09-10 the row was drawn only when the field above had been typed
    in by hand, so the mediums read off the collection were computed and then
    thrown away — every teacher page but one showed a name and nothing else.
  endcomment

  comment
    The artist comp carries a short line of Cedarville script under the name.
    Its content in Figma is lorem, and leaving the field blank left 34 artist
    pages with nothing but a name. When "use the collection description" is on
    the line is taken from the collection's own description — the FIRST
    SENTENCE only, because a full bio set in a cursive face is unreadable and
    the comp shows three short lines.

    Off by default, so the teacher pages (which already print the description
    in rb-script-statement further down) do not say the same thing twice.
  endcomment
  assign script = section.settings.script
  if script == blank and section.settings.script_from_description and collection.description != blank
    assign plain = collection.description | strip_html | strip | replace: '&nbsp;', ' '
    assign first = plain | split: '. ' | first | strip
    if first != blank
      unless first contains '.'
        assign first = first | append: '.'
      endunless
      comment
        A handful of bios open with a sentence of 200 characters or more, which
        is a paragraph however it is set. Cutting on a word rather than at a
        character count keeps the tail readable; anything shorter is left whole,
        so the common case never loses its last word to a truncation.
      endcomment
      assign first_words = first | split: ' '
      if first_words.size > 24
        assign script = first | truncatewords: 22
      else
        assign script = first
      endif
    endif
  endif

  comment
    The comp's script line is 55 characters set over three lines. A real bio's
    first sentence runs to twice that and, at the comp's size, towered to eight
    lines of cursive down the left of the page. So the line steps down through
    three sizes as it lengthens and takes a wider measure with it, which holds
    every page at the comp's three-line shape instead of holding its type size.
  endcomment
  assign script_len = script | strip_html | size
  assign script_tier = 1
  if script_len > 70
    assign script_tier = 2
  endif
  if script_len > 105
    assign script_tier = 3
  endif

  assign show_tags = false
  if tags.size > 0
    case section.settings.tags_mode
      when 'always'
        assign show_tags = true
      when 'never'
        assign show_tags = false
      else
        if script == blank
          assign show_tags = true
        endif
    endcase
  endif

  comment
    The design pairs one of the person's works, running off the right edge,
    with their black-and-white portrait set into it. Both come from the
    collection so that forty person pages are right from one shape:

      portrait — the collection's own image, which in this store is the photo
                 of the person;
      artwork  — the first piece in the collection that is not that same photo.

    A collection with nothing but the portrait falls back to showing it large
    with no inset, because the same picture twice reads as a mistake.
  endcomment
  assign art = section.settings.image
  assign portrait = section.settings.portrait
  if portrait == blank
    assign portrait = collection.image
  endif
  if art == blank
    for item in collection.products limit: 8
      if item.featured_image != blank and item.featured_image != portrait
        assign art = item.featured_image
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  if art == blank
    assign art = portrait
    assign portrait = blank
  endif

  comment
    2026-09-10, client ("Individual Artist Page — remove grey squares and just
    have artist photo"): the black-and-white inset reads as a grey square sitting
    on the work. Same note they gave for the artists index, and the index cards
    answered it the same way — see media_mode on rb-artist-cards.

      artwork_inset — Hanre's comp, the work with the portrait set into it;
      portrait      — the photo alone, filling the box, no inset;
      artwork       — the work alone, no inset.

    Kept as a setting rather than a deletion so the comp is one click away, and
    so teacher pages (which still follow the comp) are not dragged along.

    An artist with no photo keeps their artwork instead of an empty box — the
    same rule the cards use, and Careisha Esperanza and Danielle Byrne rely on it.
  endcomment
  assign media_mode = section.settings.media_mode
  if media_mode == 'portrait' and portrait != blank
    assign hero_image = portrait
    assign media_is_photo = true
    assign show_inset = false
  elsif media_mode == 'artwork' or media_mode == 'portrait'
    assign hero_image = art
    assign media_is_photo = false
    assign show_inset = false
  else
    assign hero_image = art
    assign media_is_photo = false
    assign show_inset = true
    if portrait == blank
      assign show_inset = false
    endif
  endif

  comment
    The store already keeps per-person socials in the booking_app.socials shop
    metafield, keyed by the handleized display name — the same key
    snippets/social-links.liquid uses. Reading it here means an artist or
    teacher page shows the right Instagram without anyone filling in 40
    templates by hand.
  endcomment
  if name != blank
    assign social_key = name | handleize
    assign person_socials = shop.metafields.booking_app.socials.value[social_key]
  endif

  comment
    "See Portfolio" on a teacher page belongs on that person's ARTIST
    collection. Someone who both teaches and exhibits has two collections
    sharing one title — "Susan Orpen" as susan-orpen-1 (teacher) and
    susan-orpen (artist).

    Handleizing the title to find the twin looked obvious and was wrong:
    "Zara-Leigh Farinha" handleizes to zara-leigh-farinha, which is a stale
    collection, while her real artist page is zara-leigh. So the twin is found
    through the work instead — the two collections share products, so the
    first collection on one of this person's pieces that carries the same
    title under a different handle is the one wanted.

    A teacher who sells nothing here but keeps a portfolio of their own falls
    back to that site — Susan Orpen shows work at susanorpenfineart.co.za and
    has no collection on this store, so without the fallback her page carries
    her name and nothing else. A teacher with neither resolves to nothing and
    the button is dropped rather than left pointing at "#".
  endcomment
  assign portfolio_url = section.settings.button_link
  if portfolio_url == blank and collection != blank
    for item in collection.products limit: 4
      for sibling in item.collections
        if sibling.handle != collection.handle and sibling.title == collection.title
          assign portfolio_url = sibling.url
          break
        endif
      endfor
      if portfolio_url != blank
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  if portfolio_url == blank and person_socials != blank
    assign portfolio_url = person_socials.website
  endif
  assign portfolio_external = false
  if portfolio_url contains '://'
    assign portfolio_external = true
  endif
  assign show_portfolio = false
  if section.settings.button_label != blank and portfolio_url != blank
    assign show_portfolio = true
  endif

  assign social_url = section.settings.social_url
  if social_url == blank and person_socials != blank
    assign social_url = person_socials.instagram
  endif
-%}

<style>
  {% comment %}
    Measured off both comps at their 1920 frame: the artwork runs from 47.6%
    to the right edge and is 790px tall, and it is flush with the top of the
    section — there is no band of white above it. So the section carries no
    vertical padding of its own; the artwork sets the height and the text
    column centres against it.

    This is the picture box the CLASS hero was matched to on 2026-08-30 — the
    height lives in --rb-hero-media-h so the two sections cannot drift apart.
  {% endcomment %}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph {
    background: {{ section.settings.background }};
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: {{ section.settings.text_width }}fr {{ 100 | minus: section.settings.text_width }}fr;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0;
    padding-block: 0;
  }
  {% comment %}
    Both comps set the text as one block whose lines share a left edge, with
    the block itself centred in its column — so the wrapper centres and the
    inner column carries the alignment. Centring each line instead would let
    the name, the script and the icon row drift apart.
  {% endcomment %}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__text {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    padding-inline: var(--rb-gutter);
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__inner {
    min-width: 0;
    text-align: {{ section.settings.align }};
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__name {
    color: {{ section.settings.name_color }};
    font-size: clamp(38px, 4.79vw, 92px);
    /* both comps break the name after the first word; 8ch was wide enough to
       keep "Kerri Sassen" on one line at this size */
    max-width: 7ch;
    {% if section.settings.align == 'center' %}margin-inline: auto;{% endif %}
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__script {
    margin-top: clamp(12px, 1.25vw, 24px);
    color: {{ section.settings.script_color }};
    line-height: 1.2;
    /* the comp wraps this line three times inside the text block, and the
       three steps below hold that shape as the sentence gets longer — see
       script_tier above. Each pair is sized at the 1920 frame. */
    {%- case script_tier -%}
      {%- when 3 -%}
        font-size: clamp(17px, 1.46vw, 28px);
        max-width: clamp(280px, 27.1vw, 520px);
      {%- when 2 -%}
        font-size: clamp(18px, 1.77vw, 34px);
        max-width: clamp(260px, 22.9vw, 440px);
      {%- else -%}
        font-size: clamp(19px, 2.08vw, 40px);
        max-width: clamp(240px, 18.6vw, 357px);
    {%- endcase -%}
    {% if section.settings.align == 'center' %}margin-inline: auto;{% endif %}
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__script p { margin: 0; }

  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: clamp(8px, 0.83vw, 16px);
    margin: clamp(10px, 1.04vw, 20px) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    {% if section.settings.align == 'center' %}justify-content: center;{% endif %}
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__tag {
    font-family: var(--rb-sans);
    font-size: var(--rb-fs-body-sm);
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: {{ section.settings.tag_color }};
  }

  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__actions {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(8px, 0.83vw, 16px);
    margin-top: clamp(14px, 1.46vw, 28px);
    {% if section.settings.align == 'center' %}justify-content: center;{% endif %}
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__social {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: clamp(34px, 3.13vw, 60px);
    height: clamp(34px, 3.13vw, 60px);
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__social img { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; }

  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__media {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    /* shared with the class hero — see --rb-hero-* in saf-rebrand.css */
    height: var(--rb-hero-media-h);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #efefef;
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__media > img,
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__media > svg {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: {{ section.settings.focal_x }}% {{ section.settings.focal_y }}%;
  }
  {%- if media_is_photo -%}
    {% comment %}
      An upright photo cropped into this landscape box loses the top and bottom.
      A centred crop takes the head off, so the photo gets its own focal point —
      the same fix, and the same 35% default, as the artist index cards.
    {% endcomment %}
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__media > img {
      object-position: {{ section.settings.photo_focal_x }}% {{ section.settings.photo_focal_y }}%;
      filter: {% if section.settings.portrait_grayscale %}grayscale(1){% else %}none{% endif %};
    }
  {%- endif -%}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__portrait {
    left: {{ section.settings.portrait_x }}%;
    top: {{ section.settings.portrait_y }}%;
    width: {{ section.settings.portrait_w }}%;
    aspect-ratio: {{ section.settings.portrait_ratio }};
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      padding-block: 32px 0;
      gap: 28px;
    }
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__inner { width: 100%; }
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__name { max-width: none; }
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__script { max-width: none; }
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__media { height: auto; aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; }
    {%- if media_is_photo -%}
      {% comment %}
        4/3 is right for a landscape work; a person standing up survives an
        upright box far better, and on one narrow column there is room for it.
      {% endcomment %}
      #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ph__media { aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; }
    {%- endif -%}
  }
</style>

<div class="rb-section rb-bleed">
  <div class="rb-ph">
    <div class="rb-ph__text">
     <div class="rb-ph__inner">
      {%- if name != blank -%}
        <h1 class="rb-name rb-name--lg rb-ph__name">{{ name }}</h1>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if script != blank -%}
        <div class="rb-script rb-ph__script">{{ script }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if show_tags -%}
        <ul class="rb-ph__tags" role="list">
          {%- for tag in tags -%}
            <li class="rb-ph__tag">{{ tag | strip }}</li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if social_url != blank or show_portfolio -%}
        <div class="rb-ph__actions">
          {%- if social_url != blank -%}
            <a href="{{ social_url }}" class="rb-ph__social"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="{{ name | escape }} on Instagram">
              <img src="{{ 'saf-icon-instagram.png' | asset_url }}" alt="" width="60" height="60" loading="lazy">
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if show_portfolio -%}
            <a href="{{ portfolio_url }}" class="rb-btn rb-btn--plain rb-btn--outline"
               {% if portfolio_external %}target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>
              {{- section.settings.button_label | escape -}}
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
     </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rb-ph__media{% if media_is_photo %} rb-ph__media--photo{% endif %}">
      {%- if hero_image != blank -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign media_alt = hero_image.alt | default: name
          if media_is_photo
            assign media_alt = name
          endif
        -%}
        {{
          hero_image
          | image_url: width: 1920
          | image_tag:
            widths: '480, 700, 960, 1400, 1920',
            sizes: '(max-width: 749px) 100vw, 55vw',
            loading: 'eager',
            alt: media_alt
        }}
      {%- else -%}
        {{ 'image' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder-svg' }}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if show_inset -%}
        <div class="rb-inset rb-ph__portrait">
          {{
            portrait
            | image_url: width: 700
            | image_tag:
              widths: '240, 360, 520, 700',
              sizes: '(max-width: 749px) 40vw, 20vw',
              loading: 'eager',
              alt: portrait.alt | default: name
          }}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Rebrand person hero",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "rb-section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Heads a teacher page or an artist page. On a collection template the name and artwork fill themselves from the collection." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "name", "label": "Name",
      "info": "Blank uses the collection title." },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "script", "label": "Script line",
      "info": "Cedarville Cursive, as on the artist page." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "script_from_description", "default": false,
      "label": "Fall back to the collection description",
      "info": "With the script line blank, the FIRST SENTENCE of the collection description is set in the script face. Used on artist and teacher pages. Where the description also appears further down the page, switch on 'Skip the first sentence' in that section so it is not said twice." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "tags", "label": "Tags",
      "info": "Comma separated, e.g. Abstract, Watercolour, Photography. Blank reads the mediums off this collection's own artwork tags." },
    { "type": "select", "id": "tags_mode", "label": "Show the tags", "default": "auto",
      "options": [
        { "value": "auto", "label": "Only where there is no script line" },
        { "value": "always", "label": "Always" },
        { "value": "never", "label": "Never" }
      ],
      "info": "'Auto' hides the row wherever a script line is showing. Teacher pages are set to 'Always' — they carry the script line and the mediums together." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Actions" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "social_url", "label": "Instagram link",
      "info": "Blank uses the Instagram already saved for this person in the admin app." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "button_label", "label": "Button label",
      "info": "The teacher page uses 'See Portfolio'." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "button_link", "label": "Button link",
      "info": "Blank looks for a collection with the same title — a teacher's own artist page. The button is hidden when there is none." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Layout" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "align", "label": "Text alignment", "default": "left",
      "options": [
        { "value": "left", "label": "Left" },
        { "value": "center", "label": "Centred (artist page)" }
      ] },
    { "type": "range", "id": "text_width", "min": 25, "max": 60, "step": 1,
      "default": 48, "unit": "%", "label": "Text share of the row",
      "info": "Both comps put the artwork's left edge at 48%. The class page hero is set to the same 48, so changing it here parts the two." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Colour" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "background", "default": "#ffffff", "label": "Background" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "name_color", "default": "#e07468", "label": "Name" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "script_color", "default": "#1e1e1e", "label": "Script line" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "tag_color", "default": "#0c3642", "label": "Tags" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Picture" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "media_mode", "label": "What the picture shows", "default": "artwork_inset",
      "options": [
        { "value": "artwork_inset", "label": "Artwork with the portrait inset" },
        { "value": "portrait", "label": "Artist photo only" },
        { "value": "artwork", "label": "Artwork only" }
      ],
      "info": "Artist pages use the photo. Someone with no photo on file keeps their artwork." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "portrait_grayscale", "default": true,
      "label": "Black and white photo",
      "info": "Applies to 'Artist photo only'. The inset in the first option is always black and white, as in the design." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "photo_focal_x", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1,
      "default": 50, "unit": "%", "label": "Photo focal point — horizontal" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "photo_focal_y", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1,
      "default": 35, "unit": "%", "label": "Photo focal point — vertical",
      "info": "An upright photo is cropped into a wide box. Lower numbers keep the head." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Artwork" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Artwork",
      "info": "Blank uses the first piece in the collection." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "focal_x", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1,
      "default": 50, "unit": "%", "label": "Artwork focal point — horizontal" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "focal_y", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1,
      "default": 50, "unit": "%", "label": "Artwork focal point — vertical" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Portrait inset" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "portrait", "label": "Portrait",
      "info": "Blank uses the collection's own image, which is the photo of the person. Rendered black and white, as in the design." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "portrait_w", "min": 15, "max": 70, "step": 1,
      "default": 40, "unit": "%", "label": "Portrait width" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "portrait_ratio", "default": "1 / 1", "label": "Portrait aspect ratio" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "portrait_x", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1,
      "default": 50, "unit": "%", "label": "Portrait centre — horizontal" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "portrait_y", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1,
      "default": 48, "unit": "%", "label": "Portrait centre — vertical" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Rebrand person hero" }]
}
{% endschema %}
